FORMAT|rational=num:den_reduced_den_positive|qsqrt5=a+br5_means_a_plus_b_times_sqrt5_with_a_b_rationals|dist_entry=cosine#count|S_k=sum_over_distribution_rows_of_count_times_Q_k(cosine)|pair_sum=N_times_S_k_equals_sum_over_ordered_pairs_x_y_of_Q_k(x.y)|json=0
RECURRENCE|start=Gegenbauer C_k^lambda with lambda equal to (n-2) over 2, so 2 lambda equals n-2|raw=k C_k(x) equals 2(k+lambda-1) x C_(k-1)(x) minus (k+2lambda-2) C_(k-2)(x); C_0 is 1, C_1 is 2lambda x|norm=C_k(1) equals binom(k+2lambda-1,k) equals binom(k+n-3,k); C_(k-1)(1) over C_k(1) is k over (k+n-3); C_(k-2)(1) over C_k(1) is k(k-1) over ((k+n-3)(k+n-4))|derived=Q_k equals C_k over C_k(1): (k+n-3) Q_k(x) equals (2k+n-4) x Q_(k-1)(x) minus (k-1) Q_(k-2)(x); Q_0 is 1, Q_1 is x|n4=(k+1) Q_k equals 2k x Q_(k-1) minus (k-1) Q_(k-2); Q_k is U_k over (k+1), Chebyshev second kind|n8=(k+5) Q_k equals (2k+4) x Q_(k-1) minus (k-1) Q_(k-2)|n24=(k+21) Q_k equals (2k+20) x Q_(k-1) minus (k-1) Q_(k-2)|at_1=if Q_(k-1)(1) and Q_(k-2)(1) are 1 then Q_k(1) is (2k+n-4-(k-1)) over (k+n-3), which is 1|verified_here=both routes evaluated at every cosine and at 1; see CHECK route_agreement and Q_k_at_1_eq_1|json=0
